// KNOWN SILENT-WRONG (open) — the monomorphization residue's LOWER-TIME face,
// the sibling of mn-generic-nested-lambda.mn. NOT gated: compiles clean, runs
// wrong (prints the ADDRESS: "val: 1048600", the first cell past heap base).
//
// Two stacked causes, both measured 2026-07-22:
//   1. No twin is demanded: the worthiness witness is binop-only (arith /
//      compare / eq on a free-floored operand), and to_string(x) is a CALL —
//      the scan never counts it, so describe stays floor.
//   2. Even a twin could not fix it: to_string dispatches at LOWER
//      (lower_to_string_dispatch reads the operand's floor type and commits a
//      word-show path into the LowIR), and the emit-time spec_wty bracket
//      cannot re-make a decision lower already minted. The same holds for
//      hash(x) — every LOWER-time type dispatch inside a generic body is
//      invisible to emit-time specialization.
//
// The ULTIMATE is band D's own peer (Hβ.fold.show-leaf / .compare-hash-leaf):
// synthesize the show/hash leaves as lowered LFns whose type reads happen at
// EMIT — then the bracket specializes them like every other read, and the
// sensitivity witness widens to cover the call. Until then this face is
// documented here; the sound forms are to_string at a concrete call site or
// an annotated parameter.
fn describe(x) with Memory + Alloc = "val: " ++ to_string(x)

fn main() with Memory + Alloc = {
  if describe(2.5) == "val: 2.5000000000000000" { 42 } else { 1 }
}
